# ============================================================================
# MA et al. PCL/CALB
# NIWA SINGLE-D SPATIAL LATTICE: THICKNESS STUDY
# ============================================================================
#
# NIWA mechanism (unchanged):
#
#   E + C  --k2--> ZC
#   ZC     --kc--> E + D
#   ZC     --km--> E + A
#   E + A  --k1--> ZA
#   ZA     --ka--> E + D
#   D      --ke--> P + V
#
# Local state constraint:   C + A + ZC + ZA + D + V = 1
# Local porosity:           phi = V
# Face diffusivity:         D_E,f = De0 * max(phi_L, phi_R)
#
# Each grade uses its own fitted NIWA PDE parameters and initial
# crystallinity, transferred unchanged to every thickness. No refitting.
#
# Geometry convention
# -------------------
# Full specimen: 30 mm x 10 mm x thickness. The CA resolves the 2-D
# cross-section thickness (x) x 10 mm width (y). The 30 mm length is
# out-of-plane.
#
# Changes relative to the previous version of this study
# ------------------------------------------------------
# 1) Grid: reference lattice is REF_NX = 30 rows across 0.30 mm
#    (0.010 mm cells), matching the Chapter 7 CA. The physical cell size is
#    held fixed, so thickness, not resolution, is the controlled variable.
#
# 2) Exposure: by default enzyme is prescribed on the two film faces only
#    (x = 0 and x = thickness) with zero flux at the 10 mm edges
#    (EXPOSE_EDGES = False). This isolates through-thickness erosion; with
#    all four sides exposed, edge attack grows with thickness and confounds
#    the comparison. Set EXPOSE_EDGES = True to recover the Ch7 boundary
#    condition.
#
# 3) Simulation time is T_END = 20 h for every thickness, the duration of
#    the Ma et al. experiment. The parameters were calibrated on 0 to 20 h,
#    so no case is extrapolated in time. t25/t50/t75 are reported only where
#    they are reached within 20 h (NaN otherwise).
#
# 4) pH is mass-consistent. The bath volume is the experimental one, so the
#    released product is scaled by the film mass relative to the 0.30 mm
#    reference film:
#        P_bath = (released mass fraction) * (h / REF_THICKNESS)
#    The linear pH law pH = pH0 - alpha * P_bath was calibrated only for
#    P_bath up to about one reference film; beyond PH_VALID_P_MAX the pH is
#    reported as NaN instead of being extrapolated.
#
# 5) New output: eroded depth per face, d(t) = (WL/100) * h / 2, and the
#    erosion-front velocity (slope of d(t) over the fixed window 1 to 8 h,
#    the same for every thickness). For a surface-erosion model d(t) should
#    collapse across thicknesses until the fronts approach the mid-plane.
#
# 6) Plots have no titles; grade and thickness information is in the
#    legend and file names.
#
# Stochasticity enters only through the random initial C/A morphology; the
# lattice update itself is deterministic (expected fractional masses).
# ============================================================================


